      text: "Every one who has had to do with others, knows that one of the most painful and trying duties of life is to listen patiently to others, when they go on speaking on subjects to which we are quite indifferent, or which we have heard a hundred times before. And yet this is a duty which we owe to all men, and which we are bound to perform with cheerfulness; for we know not what God may be working in their hearts, of which their words, however unworthy they may seem, are the imperfect index.",
